# Nice Touch – Project Overview

## Stack

- **React 19** with TypeScript (strict mode), functional components only
- **Vite 7** for bundling; `@vitejs/plugin-react` + `@tailwindcss/vite`
- **Tailwind CSS v4** for all styling — no separate CSS files except `index.css` (global resets/tokens) and `LiquidEther.css` (scoped to the WebGL background)
- **React Router v7** (`BrowserRouter` + nested routes via `<Outlet />`)
- **Three.js** powers the `LiquidEther` fluid background
- **HubSpot** embedded forms (loaded via `<script>` tag injection)
- **Stripe** for checkout (direct links in `src/data/pricing.ts`)
- Package manager: **npm**; path alias `@/` maps to `src/`

## Folder Structure

```
src/
  App.tsx                     # Route tree only — no logic
  main.tsx                    # Entry point
  index.css                   # Tailwind directives + CSS custom properties
  assets/
    icons/                    # SVG icons (apple, windows, discord, linkedin, youtube)
    images/                   # PNG images (logos, app badges)
  backgrounds/
    LiquidEther.tsx            # WebGL fluid — do not modify without care
    LiquidEther.css
  components/
    layout/
      Layout.tsx               # Shell: LiquidEther + Header + <Outlet /> + Footer
      Header.tsx               # Nav links from data/navigation.ts, social from data/social.ts
      Footer.tsx               # Footer links, social, copyright
    ui/
      Button.tsx               # Reusable button (variant: primary/secondary/ghost, size: sm/md/lg)
      Container.tsx            # Max-width content wrapper
    GetAppModal.tsx            # HubSpot modal form
    DownloadCard.tsx           # macOS / Windows download buttons
    NewsletterForm.tsx         # HubSpot newsletter embed
  data/
    navigation.ts              # NAV_LINKS array — single source of truth for nav
    pricing.ts                 # PLANS, CHECKOUT_LINKS, detectCurrency(), formatPrice()
    social.ts                  # SOCIAL_LINKS, CONTACT_EMAIL
  hooks/
    useReleases.ts             # Fetches release data from GitHub JSON
  pages/
    Home.tsx
    Pricing.tsx
    Download.tsx
    Newsletter.tsx
    NotFound.tsx
```

## Routing

All routes are children of the `<Layout />` route. The route table lives in
`src/routes.tsx` (the single source of truth consumed by `App.tsx`, the
prerenderer, and the sitemap generator). To add a new page:
1. Create `src/pages/MyPage.tsx` (include an `<SEO title=… description=… path=…/>` and exactly one `<h1>`)
2. Add an entry to `ROUTES` in `src/routes.tsx` (with a `sitemapPriority` so it lands in the sitemap)
3. Add a nav entry to `src/data/navigation.ts` if it should appear in the header/footer

## SEO / prerendering (do not break)

- The site is prerendered at build time: `npm run build` runs `vite build`,
  then `vite build --ssr src/entry-server.tsx`, then `scripts/prerender.mjs`
  which writes one static `dist/<route>/index.html` per route plus
  `dist/404.html` and `dist/sitemap.xml`, and finally
  `scripts/verify-prerender.mjs` which fails the build on missing/duplicate
  titles, descriptions, canonicals, H1s, or invalid JSON-LD.
- Components must stay SSR-safe: never touch `window`/`document` at module
  level or during render — only inside `useEffect` or event handlers, or
  behind a `typeof window !== 'undefined'` guard.
- Per-page meta is owned by `src/components/ui/SEO.tsx` (react-helmet-async).
  `index.html` must NOT contain page-specific title/meta — only the
  `<!--app-head-->` / `<!--app-html-->` placeholders.
- Site-wide Organization/WebSite JSON-LD lives in `src/components/ui/SiteSchema.tsx`.
- `_headers` (repo root) sets security + caching headers on Sevalla; `public/robots.txt` excludes `/press/assets/`.
